[[Category:Tmp_xyobj(neg)]]

Deer are hoofed ruminant mammals related to [[Reindeer]].
Deer are found in groups ranging in sizes of 1-5 on any of the forest terrains. They run at a running speed of 3, which means a hearthling will be unable to outrun them barefoot on forest terrain, should they chase you after being aggroed.
Deer should not be confused with [[Moose]] which are quite a bit stronger. Deer are a brighter brown color and are quite a bit less bulky than [[Moose]].

==Combat==

===Behaviour===

Deer are passive until you aggro them. They're quite quick, so you should fight on horseback or prepare to brawl at a standstill. They spawn in packs of 3 to 5 but do not fight in packs like in Legacy, they'll take you on by themselves. 

Their attacks aren't particularly tough and they have low health and armor, however they have an exceptionally high Agility stat and will easily overwhelm you with sheer attack rate, skyrocketing your openings to deal moderate damage at high speeds if you have lower Agility. They attack faster than a horse and on par with a Lynx. 

At 40-60 AGI you should be able to counteract theirs and kill them easily with a cheap sword or decent Tinker axe and Quick Barrage/Full Circle or Uppercut/Sideswipe.  

Bringing some basic armor like a shield and a leather chestplate would be wise as it lets you tank the knicks of damage they'll deal allowing you to stand and deliver without much worry about your openings.   

If you have lower Agility but enough firepower to make it through their armor, fight on a horse and retreat to recover your openings often. Their Sudden Charge can be brutal. 

